config HORIZON
	bool "Run Nintendo Switch (Horizon) programs natively"
	depends on ARM64 && MMU && SHMEM
	select RT_MUTEXES
	help
	  A Horizon system call personality for the services and loader of
	  Horizon Linux (mizu): threads of a program started with
	  horizon_execve(2) have their "svc #N" instructions (N != 0) handled
	  as Horizon SVCs, while "svc #0" stays a Linux system call. Services
	  are ordinary Linux processes that use horizon_servctl(2).

	  Horizon threads are scheduled as SCHED_FIFO (priorities 1 to 49)
	  when the process may use real-time priorities: with CAP_SYS_NICE,
	  or up to its RLIMIT_RTPRIO. Otherwise they are SCHED_NORMAL.

	  If unsure, say N.
